much about Tru64 TCP/IP (being of HP-UX history) but I have found that
99 times out of 10 a desire to disable the Nagle algorithm is
triggered by what are arguably bugs in application code.
Specifically, applications trying to write "logically associated" data
in multiple "send" calls rather than one (perhaps gathering) send.

